Okay, evaluating the **Mercedes-Benz A-Class A200 CDI**.

Similar to the A180 CDI, the 'A200 CDI' designation was used on the **second generation (W169, 2004-2012)** and the **third generation (W176, 2012-2018)** A-Class. The latest generation (W177) uses 'A200d'. Therefore, the most recent model explicitly called 'A200 CDI' is the **W176 generation (produced until 2018)**. This model offered more power than the A180 CDI.

I will evaluate this specific W176 A200 CDI model against **today's (2024) market benchmarks**. This means comparing a car designed in the early/mid-2010s to the average new car available now.

